<<
/Author (Hunter Hughes)
/CreationDate (D\07220261111152611\05505\04700\047)
/Creator (H Heuristics PDF pipeline)
/Keywords (sustainable convergence\054 global economic convergence\054 sustainable development\054 Sustainable Convergence Measurement Framework\054 SCMF\054 polycrisis resilience\054 Global South\054 emerging economies\054 technology diffusion\054 leapfrogging\054 clean energy transition\054 decoupling\054 development economics\054 scenarios to 2100)
/ModDate (D\07220261111152611\05505\04700\047)
/Producer (ReportLab PDF Library \055 www\056reportlab\056com)
/Subject (For most of the past two centuries\054 the question of whether poorer countries are catching up with richer ones has been answered with a single number\072 income per person\056 This report argues that the question needs a wider answer\054 and that convergence should be judged by how it happens as well as how fast\054 and by whether prosperity\054 environmental quality and resilience advance together\056 It develops Sustainable Convergence\054 a concept the report presents as developed by Hunter Hughes\054 Founder of H Heuristics\054 and defines it as the process through which emerging and developing economies progressively narrow economic\054 technological\054 institutional and human\055development gaps with advanced economies while pursuing environmentally sustainable\054 socially inclusive and systemically resilient development pathways\056)
/Title (Sustainable Global Economic Convergence\072 A Framework for Advancing Prosperity\054 Environmental Quality and Systemic Resilience Together)
/Trapped /False
>>
endobj
